  "interface_contracts": {
    "evidence_selection": "Full source hash is distinct from the selected excerpt hash; UTF-8 offsets, window lineage, optional one-review context lineage, bridge source binding, and canonical selection binding are persisted.",
    "ingest_recovery": "A deterministic successor receipt binds owner, operation, bridge source binding, send_external, deterministic evidence id, and deterministic extraction job id; a worker-only read verifies the complete binding after cross-database uncertainty.",
    "excerpt_retention": "The caller cannot choose retention. A send_external review excerpt receives a server-owned seven-day deadline and remains available while work is active. At the deadline, any pre-dispatch reserved or claimed attempt is first made retryable or terminal with evidence_excerpt_expired_before_dispatch; the excerpt is then redacted and no provider dispatch is authorized without evidence.",
    "worker_restart_reconstruction": "The PostgreSQL lease returns immutable source and context identifiers and hashes. A cold worker reloads the exact source from conversation authority after bridge purge; cached eligibility or selection objects are never authority.",
        "provider_dispatch": "Only a reserved call can return dispatched and authorize one network call. An already-dispatched call fails closed even when the request hash matches, so replay cannot authorize a second provider call; expired dispatched calls become outcome_unknown and are never automatically retried.",
        "terminal_proposal_replay": "Terminal proposal exact replay is guaranteed only during the 30 days before terminal proposal retention purge. After the content-bearing proposal is removed, exact replay is unavailable and the API returns proposal_retention_purged using content-free audit evidence rather than reconstructing deleted proposal content.",
        "proposal_review_cas": "Proposal hash, source hash, selected evidence hash, selection binding hash, predicate catalog semantic hash, exact decision, and canonical reason-code array must all match.",
    "semantic_identity": "SHA-256 of normalized subject key plus predicate plus structured object identity; correction may change object and therefore claim semantic key.",
    "read_claim_candidates": "Returns current owner-scoped authoritative claim and revision identity, lifecycle and policy state, catalog and evidence bindings, structured subject and object, deterministic retrieval text and retrieval_text_sha256, validity, and update time.",
    "projection": "PostgreSQL is authoritative; Qdrant receives only the current admitted projectable revision and never source_sha256. Only a strictly lower projection sequence is superseded automatically. Cold rebuild rows require the current active projectable claim, its current revision, and the exact applied upsert outbox receipt and manifest; Qdrant cannot seed rebuild truth.",
    "retrieval_score_gate": "Candidate scores are validated only to the closed normalized-dot interval and sorted deterministically. Production activation is blocked until a minimum semantic score is calibrated on an authorized holdout and bound into the retrieval policy.",
        "answer_binding": "The caller supplies claim ids, not revision ids. PostgreSQL derives exact current revision ids and hashes, reloads and renders the authorized records, persists the content-free retrieval policy envelope beside its recomputable hash, proves selection and injection manifests, rejects internal ids or hashes in provider-visible content, and persists only hashes and byte offsets after dispatch.",
        "answer_binding_retention": "Each terminal answer binding expires exactly 90 days after its one server-owned creation timestamp. A bounded worker purge first appends an exact content-free retention receipt, then deletes only that locked expired binding under a binding-specific local purge context. Exact answer replay is unavailable after retention purge.",
    "hard_delete": "A verified applied Qdrant delete is required before content purge. Reciprocal proposal and revision foreign keys use deferred NO ACTION so the closed graph is checked at commit. The immutable claim_deletion_receipt remains content-free and is not part of retention purge."
  },
